<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="two">
      <div>
        <h2>What is an enzyme?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Enzymes (E) are biological catalysts that speed up the chemical reactions keeping you alive.</p>
        <p>Without them, vital processes like digesting food and making energy would happen far too slowly for life to exist.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>They turn substrates (S) into products (P) by lowering the activation energy (E<sub>a</sub>), without changing the reaction’s overall energy (ΔG).</p>
        <p>They bond because positives (enzyme) and negatives (substrate) attract.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="steps" aria-label="Enzyme reaction path">
      <div class="step" data-step="0"><b>E + S</b><span>Enzyme meets substrate</span></div><div class="arrow">⇌</div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1"><b>ES</b><span>They bond</span></div><div class="arrow">→</div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2"><b>E + P</b><span>Enzyme is free, product is made</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

